questions.q:
Analyse how the Suryodaya class election was made free and fair. For each step, say what was done and what unfairness it prevented:
(a) the appointment of the Election Officer and the explanation of the rules;
(b) the secret ballot and the voting booths;
(c) the braille ballot paper;
(d) the sealed box and the witness at the count;
(e) the handling of the unmarked ballot.

Compare the election to the Lok Sabha with the election to a state legislative assembly under these heads:
(a) the level of governance and the issues the members mainly focus on;
(b) what the elected members are called, and one regional name for the assembly;
(c) how the winner in each constituency is decided;
(d) who forms the government afterwards and who heads it.
